{%- comment -%}
  lc-gcr-optin.liquid — Google Customer Reviews opt-in survey module.

  ⚠️ SCOPE — read before assuming this reaches buyers.

  This renders on the CUSTOMER ACCOUNT order page (`request.page_type ==
  'customers/order'`, template `templates/customers/order.json`), which is where a
  signed-in customer looks up a past order.

  It does NOT render on the post-checkout "thank you" / order-status page. That page is
  owned by Shopify Checkout, not the theme: `layout/theme.liquid` never executes there, and
  `request.page_type` has no value for it at all (the documented set is 404, article, blog,
  captcha, cart, collection, list-collections, customers/*, gift_card, index, metaobject,
  page, password, policy, product, search). `request.page_type == 'order'` — a value that
  does not exist — would silently never match.

  Practical consequence: on a store with mostly guest checkout, very few buyers ever open
  this page, so opt-in volume from here is small. The two routes that actually reach every
  buyer are the Google & YouTube channel app, or a Merchant Center order feed once the
  Shopify token gains `read_orders`. Both are written up in
  docs/GOOGLE-CUSTOMER-REVIEWS-SETUP.md.

  Estimated delivery = order date + 8 BUSINESS days. Liquid has no business-day arithmetic,
  so weekends are skipped explicitly: 8 business days is 10 calendar days when the order
  falls Mon/Tue, and 12 when it falls Wed–Sun (the run crosses a second weekend).

  Usage: {% render 'lc-gcr-optin' %}
{%- endcomment -%}

{%- if request.page_type == 'customers/order' and order != blank -%}
  {%- liquid
    assign gcr_email = order.email
    if gcr_email == blank
      assign gcr_email = order.customer.email
    endif

    assign gcr_country = order.shipping_address.country_code
    if gcr_country == blank
      assign gcr_country = order.billing_address.country_code
    endif
    if gcr_country == blank
      assign gcr_country = 'CA'
    endif

    comment
      %w gives 0 (Sunday) through 6 (Saturday). Orders placed Wed–Sun push the 8th
      business day past a second weekend, so they need 12 calendar days instead of 10.
    endcomment
    assign gcr_weekday = order.created_at | date: '%w' | plus: 0
    assign gcr_offset_days = 12
    if gcr_weekday == 1 or gcr_weekday == 2
      assign gcr_offset_days = 10
    endif
    assign gcr_offset_seconds = gcr_offset_days | times: 86400
    assign gcr_delivery = order.created_at | date: '%s' | plus: gcr_offset_seconds | date: '%Y-%m-%d'
  -%}

  {%- if gcr_email != blank -%}
    <script src="https://apis.google.com/js/platform.js?onload=renderGcrOptIn" async defer></script>
    <script>
      window.renderGcrOptIn = function () {
        window.gapi.load('surveyoptin', function () {
          window.gapi.surveyoptin.render({
            merchant_id: 5804673777,
            order_id: {{ order.name | json }},
            email: {{ gcr_email | json }},
            delivery_country: {{ gcr_country | json }},
            estimated_delivery_date: {{ gcr_delivery | json }}
          });
        });
      };
    </script>
  {%- endif -%}
{%- endif -%}
